This document demonstrates a Typst template for graduate theses at Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications. The template centralizes the formatting of covers, declarations, contents, headers, headings, figures, tables, equations, and references so that authors can focus on their thesis content.

All metadata and text in this example are placeholders. They contain no real names, student identifiers, supervisors, research data, or other personal information. Before submission, authors should verify the result against the latest requirements of their school and the graduate school.

